-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Booty
  Publisher   Firebird, 1984
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Booty (1984)(Firebird).z80
  MD5         0b2cb0c5a033e853d62c3a5e492f8bc0

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The game's play area has no colour clash, so none is removed: the default
  keeps the original look. The patch adds the menu, its cheats and the Next
  start-up. Game logic is unchanged. Enhanced colours, an option on the menu,
  are below.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 conversion's colours on every figure and all the
              scenery, drawn on a Layer 2 over the original screen: the
              title's ship, palm and chest, the wooden holds, keys, treasure
              and pirates. The set's own black behind everything. Its text
              keeps the game's ink. Source: Enhanced colours: Ynicky
              (Spec256).

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: the original game with Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt
              ROM (NextZXOS 26.11 safe); no game byte changed in the default,
              no hook; Enhanced colours, a menu option, off by default, from
              the Spec256 set; the tape's loading screen; eight tested cheats

  Note        Keys: menu 1 keyboard, 2 Interface 2, 3 cursor, 4 Kempston, 5
              define keys, 0 start. Keyboard: 5 left, 8 right, 7 up, 6 down, A
              through a door, M sound, P pause. The original game: every
              figure and all the scenery are whole 8x8 cells printed with
              their own attribute, so it has no colour clash to remove. 48K,
              beeper music as the original. Fits a 1MB Next, Enhanced
              included. Known issues: pace in JNext against the original,
              music off in both to compare like with like, 4 holds x 3 seeds:
              whole runs default +0.49 to +0.62, Enhanced -1.00 to +0.99
              percent; slowest 20-update stretch default +2.35, Enhanced +3.33
              percent; with music on, a note at an update boundary moves a
              stretch several percent either way. Enhanced: the menu's three
              heading lines are black on black, as in the set (black ink on
              the set's black). Missing: the hidden game has no colours in
              Enhanced (Layer 2 goes off with its cheat); natural play past a
              few holds (others by a test call); hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immune to pirates
   3  Immune to birds & rats
   4  Bombs don't explode
   5  Walk through all doors
   6  No pirates
   7  Don't throw back to start
   8  Access hidden game

  The archive's .pok for this release: eight of its entries, tested; the
  hidden game's own three need a typed value or its cheat, left out.

